The keepers before them had left notes, too. Most were practical:

- trim the wick before dusk
- *never* leave the door to the gallery unlatched
+ write down every ship, even the ones you are not sure of

The last one was underlined twice, which was how her father underlined things that mattered (see @woolf1927, p. 41).

He kept the nights in a ledger, too, as @tab:1 shows.

